<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The lord's gear ladder's lord's materials (docs/features/armour-acquisition.md, #693): one per culture
  that owns armour; a culture with none of its own uses its armour donor's (culture_marketplace_config.xml,
  armour_from). They drop after battles won and pay "The Deep Seam", and a stack of them stands in for a
  ladder rung's deeds at the armoury (armour_acquisition_config.xml, <LordsMaterials>, <LordsLadder>).

  Names and art are PLACEHOLDERS until Mike or KEYforce set them: every material wears the vanilla
  thamaskene ingot (an item's inventory icon is a render of its mesh, so new art is a mesh and texture).

  Nothing in the engine or TAOM hands them out (engine v1.5.3; the feature doc's engine facts):
    item_category="unassigned"  no trade good: no workshop makes it and no caravan buys it
    is_merchandise="false"      battle loot, plunder, wreckage and the tournament pools skip it
    value 500 or more           the hideout's night loot pool takes any Goods item up to a theoretical
                                market value of 4750 (ten times its value) without checking the flag,
                                so 475 or more is what keeps a material out of it
    no culture                  CultureMarketplace pools only items with a culture
  A stack the player sells leaves the usual ways: a town slowly consumes it (a zero-demand category
  still gets 1% of the town's prosperity as daily demand), and the vanilla Trade Proposal incident may
  offer for it. Like vanilla's XML non-food goods, the rows carry only the Civilian flag.
-->
<Items>
  <Item id="taom_lords_material_gondor" name="{=taom_lm_gondor}Númenórean Steel" mesh="thamaskene_steel"
        item_category="unassigned" value="500" weight="0.5" is_merchandise="false" Type="Goods">
    <Flags Civilian="true" />
